# The binary `go build ./cmd/rashomon

# Agent and editor state, which is per-machine and not this project's.
/.claude/` drops in the repository root. The module
# IS the repository root, so the output lands beside go.mod as a ten-megabyte
# file named exactly `rashomon` -- and the README tells a contributor to run
# that command, then `./rashomon watch`, because watch has to be run from a
# built binary. `*.exe` already covered the Windows spelling; this covers the
# one everyone else gets. Anchored, so it cannot swallow a source path.
/rashomon
coverage.out
coverage.html

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

.claude/settings.local.json
